# Introduction to Thinking Critically About AI

Let’s dive into the first section of this professional learning module. This section introduces the structure, goals, tools, and instructional approaches that students experience throughout the unit.

<div style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 20px; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom:0px">
    <div style="width: 70%;">
        <p style="line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px;">
            In this section, you will:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin-left: 20px; line-height: 1.6;">
            <li style="line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px;">
                Describe the structure and goals of the Thinking Critically About AI unit
            </li>
            <li style="line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px;">
                Explain how students investigate AI systems through testing, evidence collection, and reflection
            </li>
            <li style="line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px;">
                Identify the major concepts students explore, including prompting, bias, verification, privacy, and responsible AI use
            </li>
            <li style="line-height: 1.5; font-size: 16px;">
                Explore the digital tools students use to build and revise their Generate and Judge Guide
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
